WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Can a vivid memory still contain an error?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
Recall is more than pressing play.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
In 1974, researchers changed question wording.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Viewers watched a vehicle event, then answered questions.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
Wording affected some later reports.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Experience leaves traces, not a complete recording.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Later information may join the reconstruction.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Inferences can fill some of the gaps.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
The puzzle is a metaphor for this process.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
Confidence is a feeling, not a guarantee.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
It does not make every memory unreliable.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
It cannot dismiss someone’s important experience.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
Check dates, photos and contemporaneous records.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Ask openly: what do you remember?

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
External records also have limits.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
When memories differ, leave room to check.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Memory deserves both attention and careful checking.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
Give the past another reliable reference.
